The Gherkin representation is chosen for its alignment with the user-facing aspects of the requirements and its readability, which is beneficial for capturing the behavior of the system from a user's perspective. It is less complex and more straightforward for writing and understanding tests. On the other hand, xUnit Test Cases are selected for their ability to directly address the detailed functional and constraint requirements at the code level, ensuring thorough testing of the integration and data flow between the different components of the system. This choice balances the need for both high-level behavioral specifications and low-level code-level testing, providing a comprehensive approach to validating the requirements.
